cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CADCLAW in your research or engineering work, please cite it as below."
title: "CADCLAW: Automated assembly and validation framework for STEP-based CAD"
abstract: >-
  CADCLAW builds and verifies STEP CAD assemblies. It compiles a declarative
  assembly spec into a STEP file, placing authored STEP parts by connector
  frames and datum chains rather than hand-typed coordinates, and emits a
  design inventory, a model-derived BOM, review-view renders, and step-by-step
  assembly sequences. It then runs automated gates over the result: inventory,
  interference, adjacency, dimensional, orientation, floating-part, and
  color/material checks, structural analysis (beam deflection, motor torque
  budget, belt tension), tolerance stacking (worst-case / RSS / Monte Carlo),
  STEP-vs-STEP parity, and a BOM-vs-CAD audit. Findings carry severity,
  evidence, and a confidence budget rather than bare pass/fail. CADCLAW places
  parts authored in external CAD; it does not generate geometry. Includes an
  MCP server exposing both the assembly and validation tools to AI coding
  assistants, with rendered review views returned as inline images so an agent
  can visually verify each assembly round.
type: software
